  <cac:TenderingProcess>
    
    <cbc:Description languageID="ENG">A next generation of sequencing instruments (NGS) shall be procured at the Molecular Biology Laboratory. We would like an instrument with medium sequencing capacity, high accuracy, good user friendliness and good flexibility. The instrument is primarily intended for use in population genetic analyses, replacing SNP analyses (Maldi-Tof) and micro-satellite analysis (capillary lecturer lecturer). In prioritised order, these areas of use are planned for the instrument that shall be procured: genotyping by sequencing (GBS, 1), species identification by metabarcoding (2), CRISPR mutant sequencing (3) for saint resequencing (4), and methylation analysis (5). Molecular biology laboratory genotypes 25-30,000 samples per annum, and our standard SNP analysis includes as usual 50 to 200 markers. Based on intended use, we want an instrument that can deliver data with high base accuracy and with a low error rate, deliver a high number of readings per run and provide high sequencing coverage.</cbc:Description>
    <cbc:ProcedureCode listName="procurement-procedure-type">open</cbc:ProcedureCode>
    <cac:NoticeDocumentReference>
